@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.24.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.24.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.24.0 (2026-11-24): Chapter 10 page story done. The first page test run failed one check: the shelve example could not run in the browser (no dbm module there) and the Mad Libs result differed from the slide because the program ended with a value that the page prints. Source 1.1.0 repairs both (a hidden stand-in for dbm used only when dbm is missing; the Mad Libs program saves before it prints), so deck 4.1.0 and manifest 1.3.0 replace deck 4.0.0 and manifest 1.2.0 as the chapter 10 deck and manifest of this lineage; the 4.0.0 files stay unchanged."""@en .

ex:TK11_Page_10_Build backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Page 03-materials/ch10/page/sen0414_ch10_page_v9_21_0.html built from template 9.53.6, page data 2.29.0 and builder 4.18.3 (all unchanged since chapter 11), manifest 03-materials/ch10/page/chapter_code_ch10_v1_3_0.json (written by chapter_deck_build_v2_8_0.py from 08-tooling/ch10-deck/spec_v4_1_0 and source 03-materials/ch10/source/ch10_code_source_v1_1_0.json). Deck 03-materials/ch10/SEN0414_Ch10_ReadingWritingFiles_3e_v4_1_0.pptx rebuilt from the same spec (41 slides, 18 codes); its checks are in 08-tooling/ch10-deck/logs_v4_1_0 (code check C1+C2+C4+C5 0 findings, deck standard 13 of 13, overlap, reader notes, story prose, fit, layout and notes clean). Page 9.20.0 and deck 4.0.0 stay unchanged." .
ex:TK11_Page_10_Verify backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Logs in 08-tooling/ch10-page/logs_v9_21_0: code check C1+C2+C3+C4+C5 on source, deck, manifest and page: 18 examples, 0 findings. Full page test 9.39.0 in a browser: exit 0, 412 features passed, 0 failed; its chapter-code step opened and ran all 18 examples with a visual result. A first run of the same page (built from source 1.0.0) failed that step on shelve (no dbm in the browser) and was repaired as described in the comment above; a separate run of all 18 examples showed the chip same result as on the slide for each. Open point: the page's per-concept examples still come from the old deck transcript and are reported to the Owner." .
ex:ST11_Page_10 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Criterion met for chapter 10: the page shows, explains and runs all 18 codes of the deck, equal to the deck, in one place." .
